PART 0 -- THE GUARD.  CLASS DECLARED, TESTED AGAINST MEMBERS IT HAS NOT SEEN
==============================================================================
CLASS CLAIMED: any ANCHORED DEPTH-CAPPED search that mis-reports the verdict
  'endpath(G,w) >= K' -- by reporting a witness that is not an induced path, is
  not anchored at w, or is short; or by blocking the wrong set at ANY depth.
GUARD = (i) an independent checker re-verifies EVERY returned witness
  (distinctness, anchoring, exact order, inducedness from a freshly built
  adjacency matrix), and (ii) on n <= 13 an independent SUBSET-ENUMERATION
  oracle recomputes the anchored value and must agree with the verdict.
UNSEEN MEMBERS USED AS THE TEST: 'offbyone' (accepts at K-1 vertices) and
  'anchordrift' (searches from the wrong root).  r34's guard was written for
  the ZERO-step defect, r35's real defect was the ONE-step defect, r36's unseen
  member was LATE-BLOCKING -- none of them is a length or an anchor defect.

